  "id": "screwit",
  "neon": "#7dff6a",
  "note": "SCREW IT — the chemical supply on Ironside Street. A trade counter with a works behind it.\n\nThe plant is the building. What a chem supply is for happens above the parapet: the scrubber that\ntakes what comes off the drums, and the stack that puts the rest over the roofs. The stack is\ntaller than the scrubber because a fume stack has to clear everything near it, and on this street\nthat is the Embassy's shoulder two doors down. It is the second vertical on Ironside after the\ncrane at Salvage Rites, and a different shape on purpose.\n\nThe tile's prose: stock stacked to the roofline with drums, sacks and racked threaded rod, a yellow\nhazard chevron round the door, and FASTENERS, SOLVENTS AND WHATEVER ELSE under the wordmark. So the\ndoor has yellow posts and a striped kerb, and the stock shows over the parapet as stacked drums, a\nrow of sacks and a rack of threaded rod. Steel piers divide the front into the counter and the\nshutter.\n\nA works doesn't sign itself (see UNSIGNED_TRADE); it carries a placard and a unit number. This one\nalso sells over a counter, which is the stated exception, so it carries both.",
  "pal": "ty_giardia",
